  "summary": "Four documents directly apply boosted decision-tree ensembles to energy (electricity consumption) forecasting. [V0133] (Adebayo et al., 2026) uses boosted decision-tree ensembles on the GridWatch dataset, achieving 0.73 AUROC. [V0135] (Chen et al., 2019) applies boosted decision-tree ensembles to the FireScope dataset, reporting accuracy of 0.87. [V0134] (Brennan et al., 2018) evaluates boosted decision-tree ensembles on ProtMap, obtaining F1=0.80. [V0136] (Duarte et al., 2020) reports MAE of 0.94 on ChurnBench using boosted decision-tree ensembles. As a fifth entry, [V0126] (Haddad et al., 2025) addresses electricity consumption prediction but uses self-attention encoder models rather than gradient boosted trees, making it the least directly relevant of the five; it is included only because no other on-topic gradient-boosted-tree document remains. Documents mentioning boosted decision-tree ensembles for electricity consumption only in a prior-work sentence (e.g., [V0099], [V0073], [V0049], [V0041], [V0034]) are excluded as they do not constitute direct applications.",
